solutions.body:
If a square is green, the square above it and the square to its right must also be green. So:
- bottom-left green forces everything green;
- top-left green forces top-right green;
- bottom-right green forces top-right green.

Possible green sets: none; top-right; top-left + top-right; bottom-right + top-right; top-left + top-right + bottom-right; all four. That is $6$.

**Answer: (B) 6**
